From 4bbe98115afa53d99b2c0266c985491118506d21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akira TAGOH <akira@tagoh.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:25:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Detect monospace grid fonts the advance heuristic missed

FcFreeTypeSpacing() keyed off the first three distinct advances, so a
monospace font with a few intentionally wide glyphs (2x em dash, 3x
two-em dash) was reported PROPORTIONAL -- e.g. Noto Sans Mono and Latin
Modern Mono.

When the existing rule yields proportional, additionally try to recover
fonts whose advances sit on an integer cell grid (>= 98%).  Recovery is
gated on monospaced ASCII, which keeps uniform full-width scripts and
emoji from being promoted, and stays name-independent.

Fold the advance tally into FcFreeTypeCharSet()'s glyph loop for scalable
fonts to avoid a second cmap pass.  Update the Fontations backend in
lockstep so both fc-query outputs stay identical, and add test-spacing.c
plus matching Rust cases.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Changelog: fixed
